        "procedure": "Under dry N2 using Schlenk/glovebox methods, a 100 mL Schlenk flask was charged with 0.823 g (1.30 mmol) of tris(bis(trimethylsilyl)amido)samarium and 40 mL of heptane. A solution of 0.457 g (1.30 mmol) of bis-5,5′-(2,2-dimethyl-1,3-propanediyldiimino)-2,2-dimethyl-4-hexene-3-one in 40 mL of heptane was added in one aliquot. The mixture was heated to reflux for 12 h under flowing N2. The dull-yellow mother liquor was concentrated in vacuo to 10 mL and cooled to −10 °C. Pale-yellow crystals were harvested after 4 days.",
